<title>PHILIPPINES: Petron sets 20 pct stock div.</title>
<headline>Petron sets 20 pct stock div.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil refiner Petron Corp said on Tuesday it would pay a 20 percent stock dividend but said the record date was yet to be fixed.</p>
<p>In the same disclosure to the Philippine Stock Exchange, Petron said it had approved a three-billion-peso contract, which was part of a scheduled expansion of the Bataan refinery near Manila.</p>
<p>A consortium of South Korea's Daelim Engineering Company Ltd and Japan's Mitsui Co Ltd is to be awarded the engineering procurement and construction contract for the expansion, it said.  </p>
<p>Petron is 40 percent owned by Saudi Arabia's Aramc.</p>
<p>The company also said its annual stockholders meeting would be held on April 21.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8934</p>
</text>
